WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.010
- [Mike] Hey guys! I've been
getting a ton of questions

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.280
about whether or not dogs
can get sick with COVID-19,

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.090
can they pass it on to their owners,

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.360
and while I'm not a vet,

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.180
I'm gonna answer some of
those questions today,

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.141
as well as giving you some
really important truths

00:00:12.141 --> 00:00:14.583
about how to keep you, and your pets, safe

00:00:14.583 --> 00:00:16.100
during a time of quarantine.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.280
To make this happen,

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.260
I've collabed with someone really special

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.389
It's my good friend

00:00:20.389 --> 00:00:23.440
(goofy voice) Da Bear Pup

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.590
Hi (inaudible)

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.282
Definitely stayed tuned
to the end of this video

00:00:26.282 --> 00:00:29.170
cause Bear and I are gonna
open some of your packages

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:30.780
that you've sent to the P.O. Box

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.450
Yeah, it's like a pandemic for
me to visit the Post Office

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:34.610
to pick up my packages.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:37.430
All right, let's get started with Tip #1

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.920
From what we know now,
there is no evidence

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.920
showing that dogs can
get sick with COVID-19.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:44.210
There have been a few dogs that have

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.800
tested positive for COVID,

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.000
but it's been thought
that the reason they're

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.650
testing positive is they
have some of the virus

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.310
on their mouth, on their
nose, likely from the owners

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:55.610
that they've licked who
were COVID positive.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.921
That being said, if you have COVID-19,

00:00:57.921 --> 00:01:00.649
definitely do your part by
staying away from your pet

00:01:00.649 --> 00:01:01.640
just in case.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:02.570
#2

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:05.030
Dogs like humans, need a routine.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.820
They like to be fed at the same times,

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:09.290
walked at the same times,
played with at the same times.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.724
The more you can stick to this routine,

00:01:10.724 --> 00:01:12.961
the better behavior you're
going to get from your pup.

00:01:12.961 --> 00:01:13.900
#3

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.460
social distancing,
applies not only to you,

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:17.640
but to your pup as well.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.240
When I walk bear, everybody
wants to play with him.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.810
But now more than ever, I
have to respectfully ask

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.230
that people stay six feet away.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.640
God for bid, they sneezed
or coughed on their hand,

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.010
gotten the virus on their hands,

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:31.100
pet Bear, I pet him and
transfer the virus to my body.

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:31.933
It's a no go.

00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:33.570
Try and do your best to keep your pets

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.403
away from other people.

00:01:34.403 --> 00:01:35.630
#4

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.080
Say no to dog parks.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.830
I love watching Bear play with other pups,

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:42.140
especially small ones, like
little French Bulldogs,

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.540
but during a time like this,
the last thing you want

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.380
is one of the dogs, who potentially

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.531
licked one of their owners who has COVID,

00:01:48.531 --> 00:01:51.150
then plays with your dog,
and then brings the virus

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:51.983
home to you.

00:01:51.983 --> 00:01:53.060
#5

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:54.800
Wipe your pups paws.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.700
Now this one is more on
the really safe side.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.670
If you have someone elderly in your home,

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.230
or someone who's immunocompromised,

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:03.570
and you really want to take
that extra step to be careful,

00:02:03.570 --> 00:02:05.020
go ahead and wipe those paws down.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.290
Remember, these respiratory droplets

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:08.010
that people release into the air

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.255
eventually make their way to the ground.

00:02:09.255 --> 00:02:11.079
And if your pups been
walking around on the street,

00:02:11.079 --> 00:02:12.999
they can potentially
bring that virus home.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.450
#6

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.480
Keep an eye out for stressed out pups.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.140
With kids being home from school,

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:19.480
many people out of work,

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:21.250
dogs are getting a lot more play time.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.800
And while initially that's a good thing,

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.240
sometimes it can tire them out.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:27.730
They also do a great job at
picking up on our body language.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:28.980
You may feel stressed out,

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.280
but you think you're not showing it,

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.620
trust me your dog knows.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.630
Some ways dogs show stress is by yawning,

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.880
acting erratically, or
even having accidents

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.440
after being properly potty trained.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:41.150
In those scenarios, give
your dogs a time out

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:42.780
Put them in their crate, or safe space

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:43.613
for them to chill out.

00:02:43.613 --> 00:02:44.910
#7

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.930
Call for reinforcements if you're sick.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.470
The last thing you should be doing is

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:51.220
leaving your home if you're
experiencing COVID-19 symptoms.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.939
But remember, your pup needs daily walks.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.920
So ask a friend or loved one
to take the pup off your hands

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.287
until you recover.

00:02:57.287 --> 00:02:58.120
#8

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.840
Consider a telly visit for your pet.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.970
Many veterinary practices
across the nation

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.410
have been offering these telly visits.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.780
So call ahead to your vet

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.914
just like you do with your family doctor.

00:03:06.914 --> 00:03:08.030
#9

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:09.290
Don't overfeed your pup.

00:03:09.290 --> 00:03:11.090
You don't want your pup becoming obese,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.950
and then increasing risks of
all sorts of health problems.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.999
It's very easy when you're
spending a lot of time at home

00:03:15.999 --> 00:03:18.450
to really increase the amount
of treats you're giving.

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:19.283
Don't do that.

00:03:19.283 --> 00:03:21.740
Treats should make up only 10% or less

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.000
of a pet's diet.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:23.890
#10

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.050
Train your pup.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.610
Know that a well-trained
dog is a happy dog.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.310
And there's a few tips
I have for you on that.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.660
First, keep the training session short.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.020
Dogs perform better that way.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.790
Two, use positive, not
negative, reinforcement.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:37.360
And finally, if you need help,

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.190
don't be afraid to contact a dog trainer

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.917
because there are virtual
options available.

00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:43.553
